course: dictionary
lesson: 9824
title: Sweetheart and its many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is meant. «Come here, sweetheart» is what a parent or grandad might say to a child they love. Here sweetheart is a friendly, loving name, not a sweet and not a heart shape.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Childhood sweethearts» means two people who loved each other when they were young, so the word means a boyfriend or girlfriend. The words around it tell you the sense.
explain: «You came fifth, sweetheart — and it was brilliant.» Lucy's friend's mum is kind and comforting, even though fifth is not first. The word shows she cares about Lucy, and it helps you hear how she feels.
fact: «Sweetheart» means a person you love, a friendly name for someone you care about, or a very kind, lovely person.
fact: «Sweetheart» can mean a boyfriend or girlfriend, as in «childhood sweethearts».
fact: Grown-ups often use «sweetheart» for children they care about, as in «Thanks, sweetheart».
fact: «She's a real sweetheart» is informal and means she is very kind and lovely.
fact: Strangers calling you «sweetheart» can sound too familiar to some people, so it is a word best used with people you know well.
exercise: Lucy's mum said «You came fifth, sweetheart — and it was brilliant.» What does sweetheart show about how she feels? | She is angry that Lucy lost | She is talking about a heart shape | *She cares about Lucy and is being kind | She wants Lucy to buy her a sweet
exercise: «They were childhood sweethearts.» What does sweethearts mean here? | Two candy hearts from a shop | Children who are always sad | Friends who live next door | *People who loved each other as children, like boyfriend and girlfriend
exercise: «She's a real sweetheart.» What does this tell you about her? | She is very loud | She is very tall | She is always late | *She is very kind and lovely
test: What is «sweetheart» in «Come here, sweetheart»? | A part of the body | A shout for help | A type of sugary sweet | *A friendly, loving name for someone you care about
test: Why might a stranger calling you «sweetheart» upset some people? | It means they want to be your teacher | *It can sound too familiar or rude | It always means they are angry | It means they are your cousin
exam: Read this: «Thanks, sweetheart.» Which meaning fits best, and why? | *A friendly, loving name, so the speaker is warm and thankful | A heart drawn on a card, so the speaker is sad | A girlfriend, so the speaker is in love | A sweet to eat, so the speaker is hungry
